\f0\fs24 \cf2 <$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 To say that Chip Stockwell was the size of a Grizzly Bear and an ice cream truck would be an exaggeration, but not by much. And he filled the doorway to Hayley\'92s office, she instantly felt threatened by the notion that she might have been cast in a Stephen King novel.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 Chip held up a Post-It like he was about to perform a magic trick with it. But then he lumbered in and thumped it on Hayley\'92s desk and patted it flat.\
Hayley read:\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\sb220\qc\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 <$Scr_Cs::2>
\f1\fs22 Julius Mphasa MacGillacuddle
\f2\i\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qc\partightenfactor0

\f1\i0\fs20 \cf0 DO NOT CONNECT THROUGH SHAKTI NETWORK
\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Cs::2>
\f1\fs22 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Chip pulled a thumb drive from his overalls. \'93Plug this in and it will connect you to a dark site. You can only use it once. When you\'92re done, eat the drive.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \'93I am supposed to grind it up and sprinkle it on my porridge?\'94\
Chip shrugged. \'93It\'92s not up to me to give you dietary advice. Throw it off the lookout, if you prefer.\'94\
\'93I\'92m not going to litter for the sake of your security fears.\'94\
\'93Just destroy it. Utterly.\'94\
\'93Password?\'94\
\'93Your neighbours,\'94 Chip stated. \'93Name the daughter backwards. Twice.\'94\
Hayley took the thumb drive. \'93Does this come with a cyanide pill?\'94 She asked flippantly.\
Chip pulled a small pill bottle from his pocket and placed it on the desk. It had a child-proof cap and contained a single pill.\
Hayley\'92s eyes went wide. \'93You\'92re kidding.\'94\
Chip smiled as he retrieved the bottle. \'93Allopurinol. For my gout.\'94\
Hayley relaxed. A little. She read the note again.\
\'93The account has already expired,\'94 Chip explained. \'93But this will get you in.\'94 He tapped the thumb drive.\
\'93Thank you. I guess.\'94\
\'93No more kebabs,\'94 Chip warned, then left.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 <!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 Hayley went back to the Three Sisters\'92 townhouse, grabbed a bag she left in the family room, and took a ground car to a caf\'e9 two villages farther up in the mountains. Once there, she pulled out her tablet and switched its connection to a Skatalite account she kept for uses she euphemistically described as \'93out-of-character\'94.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 Hayley plugged Chip\'92s thumb drive in a warning popped up\'97\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\qc\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs18 \cf2 FRIDGE FORCE INTRANET\
WARNING:\
UNAUTHORISED ACCESS  INVALIDATES THE WARRANTY OF YOUR LIFE\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 Hayley blinked the memory of the last time she\'92d read something similar. Her ears still hurt. She she looked around the \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 caf\'e9 for evidence that sirens my suddenly \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
blare off.\
The pop-up presented two buttons: 
\fs20 RETREAT
\fs22  and 
\fs20 PROCEED. She tapped the second and a login pop-up appeared.
\fs22  She typed the name from the Post-It note into the account name box, then thought about the password. She recalled Bala\'92s daughter\'92s name was Shyamala, but what did Chip\'92s instructions 
\f2\i Name the daughter backwards. Twice. 
\f1\i0 mean?\
She tapped the eye icon on the password box then typed \'93Shyamala Chuglingham\'94 into the text field. She looked at it for a few moments then rearranged it to \'93mahgnilguhC alamayhS\'94. That was backwards, once. She cut and pasted to make it \'93alamayhS mahgnilguhC\'94, but that look backwards only once, too.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 Tax you, Stockwell!
\f1\i0 \
She didn\'92t know how many attempts she\'92d get at this. She tried to recall Stockwell\'92s exact instructions. Maybe they weren\'92t instructions. Maybe he just told her the password, as she requested. That sounded more like Stockwell, more direct. No puzzles required.\
Hayley typed: \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\sb220\qc\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf2  Your neighbours name the daughter backwards twice
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Her finger hovered over the 
\fs20 SUBMIT
\fs22  button, then it tapped before she really wanted it to. A file list appeared on the screen. Hayley started browsing. Among the technical and engineering analyses, she found a document that was mostly words and numbers, with a few graphs and diagrams thrown in. She searched for \'93Rotherhithe\'94.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \'93Interesting,\'94 Hayley said to herself. She noticed the first found text read as 
\f2\i Goa-Rotherhithe
\f1\i0  So did the second. And the third. Every reference she tapped treated the two places as if nothing separated them that was wider than a state border.\
Hayley went back and started scanning.\
There were maps and cross-sections of the Earth with Goa and Rotherhithe marked from different angles, surrounded by equations and comments about multi-dimensionally colocated resonant concurrency. She made it as far as an assertion that predicting events like Goa-Rotherhithe and others would require a formal multi-universal calculus that had so far resisted attempts to iron out inconsistencies in its axioms. Hayley scrolled past the discussion on the contradictions in very large set theory and how multi-universal calculus inherently needs to handle sets beyond what even Grothendieck Universe theory could handle.\
\'93It\'92s all voodoo,\'94 Hayley muttered to herself.\
The best she could extract was that relative phase mattered, geometry mattered and coherence mattered\'97change one and the region of maximum effect moved, except 
\f2\i moved
\f1\i0  was apparently the wrong word because the region was not obliged to remain anywhere sensible in three dimensions.\
She was beginning to understand why Stockwell insisted that stasis fields must never interact. For all the mathematics, Fridge Force appeared to have arrived at a hard-won superstition roughly equivalent to forbidding dragons to kiss after midnight.\
Hayley searched for something written for people who didn\'92t enjoy set theory.\
A shorter incident reconstruction opened with a photograph from Goa.\
\'93Goa?\'94\
She backed up through the reconstruction until she found something that explained why Goa was in a report about Rotherhithe at all. At the time that Rotherhithe subsided below the level of the Thames, several thousand people were partying at a quake-trance rave on the Goan coast. \
Hayley followed 
\f2\i quake-trance
\f1\i0  long enough to discover that a quasi-religious rave culture of the same name came with its own history, ceremonies, and arguments about three gods called Ludwig, Zildjian and Rickenbacker.\
\'93Rickenbacker, my arse,\'94 Hayley blurted, realising she was falling down a rabbit hole.\
A pair of patrician old ladies sipping tea with lemon at the next table gave her matching thin lips.\
Hayley backed up. Gods aside, what was so important about Goa? She should have just searched for 
\f2\i Gyges
\f1\i0 .\
No occurrence in the file.\
\'93What?\'94\
Hayley searched for 
\f2\i stasis
\f1\i0 . None of those either. She sipped her tepid latte and thought. Then she typed, \'93rotation.\'94\
She was rewarded with several hits. She stepped though until she arrived a diagram. The section title about it was, \'93Physical Configuration\'97Goa\'94.\
The diagram depicted something call the Ark and the text underneath described it. It resembled a road case commonly used for transporting stage equipment, and had sturdy castor wheels for mobility. It was described as an integral part of the sound system used at a genuine quake-trance rave. Allegedly there was only one such Ark in existence and that, without it operating in precise configuration with the bass woofers, there was no \'93quake\'94 in \'93quake-trance\'94.\
What followed was a \'93Fridge Force; In Confidence\'94 description of the mechanism inside the apparently sealed and secret Ark, which only required power connections via three external sockets.\
The were three identical assemblies. Each assembly consisted of a vinyl record turntable whose original drive had been torn out and replaced with a high-speed grinding spindle salvaged from an internal cylindrical grinder. Over the centre the turntable platters, cradles had been affixed that looked like you could snap a large coin into them and keep the coins in place.\
There were pictures\'97all bearing a legend \'93Fridge Force; In Confidence\'94\'97looking down into the Ark; presumably its lid could be removed or the Ark had been partially disassembled. Hayley looked at each picture. She had never seen a Gyges disc but imagined that\'92s was snapped into the cradle glued to the turntables in all the pictures. \
Under the pictures was the document\'92s conclusion. The Ark was the concurrently resonant apparatus that became multidimensionally colocated with Rotherhithe. Nowhere did the report 
\f2\i say 
\f1\i0  that the Ark caused Rotherhithe to sink below the Thames, but Hayley made that common-language translation anyway.\
The name \'93Rotherhithe\'94 derives from Anglo-Saxon, and probably means, \'93landing-place for cattle\'94. Whatever its origins, the district that was part of the borough of Southwark on the banks of the Thames had been the landing place of something altogether more destructive. Three spinning discs had destroyed it.\
And Johnny wanted five.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 <!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 Hayley emailed Sarah a few pictures of the turntables in the Ark, then called her from the caf\'e9.
\f4\fs26 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 After Sarah had opened the email, Hayley asked, \'93The things in the middle of the turntables: are they\'85\'94 Hayley looked about the caf\'e9 for eavesdroppers. \'93\'85discs?\'94\
There was and extended silence. Then Sarah admitted, \'93I can\'92t be sure, but I can say the colour and texture look the same as the one I\'97wait.\'94 Another pause. \'93Have you got the pictures handy?\'94\
\'93Yep. Got them right here.\'94 Stockwell\'92s thumb drive was still sticking out of her tablet on the table.\
\'93Take a look at the sixth one down. Turntable on the top right.Tell me what you see.\'94\
Hayley looked. \'93That one looks a bit different in that picture than it does in the others.\'94\
\'93Different how?\'94\
\'93Same size, same colour, but there\'92s light reflecting off the its surface close to the edge at the top.\'94\
\'93Diffracted light? Like a rainbow.\'94\
\'93Faintly, yes.\'94\
\'93It\'92s a kebab,\'94 Sarah said. \'93I\'92m pretty sure.\'94\
\'93I wonder if it\'92s Ludwig, Zildjian or Rickenbacker,\'94 Hayley said.\
\'93They have names?\'94\
\'93Maybe. I\'92ve been reading some some weird tax this afternoon.\'94\
\'93So much of what Chip said was true?\'94\
\'93The ridiculous parts seem to be the best documented.\'94\
Sarah waited.\
\'93As far as I can tell, the mathematics say Goa and Rotherhithe were thousands of kilometres apart until the kebabs decided they weren\'92t.\'94\
Another silence.\
\'93No more kababs for Johnny,\'94 Sarah said. \'93Not without more research.\'94\
\'93Good.\'94\
\'93See you tonight.\'94\
\'93Yep.\'94 Hayley disconnected.\
The thumb drive was still sticking out of her tablet. Chip had been quite specific about destroying it utterly. Hayley still wasn\'92t eating it.
